Oracle build fixes on top of the three committed beetle-psx patches.

Apply LAST, after beetle_wtrace_hook / beetle_sio_trace_hook /
beetle_cdcmd_trace_hook, against beetle-psx at 5759277b.

Two problems this closes:

1. beetle_wtrace_hook and beetle_cdcmd_trace_hook COLLIDE. The cdcmd patch
   was generated against a tree without the wtrace patch applied, so it
   re-adds g_psxrecomp_wtrace_cb / g_psxrecomp_fntrace_cb alongside its own
   cdcmd callback. Applying all three per docs/beetle-linux.md therefore
   duplicates both definitions and libretro.cpp fails to compile
   ("redefinition of g_psxrecomp_wtrace_cb"). Here the earlier duplicate
   block is dropped, keeping the cdcmd block that already declares all three.

2. runtime/src/beetle_libretro.cpp requires g_psxrecomp_rtrace_cb and
   g_psxrecomp_irq_cb, which NO committed patch provides -- the integration
   grew past the patches and the matching beetle-psx side was never captured.
   Added: typedefs + externs in psx.h, definitions in libretro.cpp, fire
   sites after each LB/LBU/LH/LHU/LW in the live interpreter (mirroring how
   the wtrace patch instruments the stores), and a rising-edge-only fire in
   IRQ_Assert (it is called on every device poll; without the edge filter the
   consumer ring fills with duplicates).

NOT sufficient to link psx-beetle on its own. That target still wants eight
more symbols no patch supplies -- beetle_core_get_guest_cycles, the five
beetle_cyc_watch_* functions, psxrecomp_cdc_irq_type, psxrecomp_dma_int_status
and retro_psxref_exc_ring_dump. Their semantics are not recoverable from this
repo, so they are deliberately NOT guessed at here (CLAUDE.md rule 14).

